---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/paths';
---
<CaseLayout title="CourtVision" eyebrow="02 / COURTVISION · COMPUTER VISION & COACHING" heading="FROM FILM TO A COACHING CONVERSATION." description="A basketball film-analysis system connecting local computer-vision processing, reviewed court replay, and a browser coaching workspace." role="Connecting the local processing and review pipeline with the coaching interface, replay tools, and deployment workflow." status="Evolving prototype / partial reviewed reconstructions" stack="Python · OpenCV · Ultralytics · Next.js · TypeScript · Cloudflare">
  <section id="question"><h2>A detection is a beginning.</h2><p>Useful coaching analysis needs more than boxes around players. The source film, court position, event, and coach’s annotation need to refer to the same moment—and that connection needs to survive processing, review, and replay.</p><figure><div class="media-frame"><video controls preload="none" playsinline poster={href('compvision/all_players.png')} aria-label="Earlier CourtVision annotated basketball sample"><source src={href('compvision/compvision-sample.mp4')} type="video/mp4" />Your browser does not support embedded video. <a href={href('compvision/compvision-sample.mp4')}>Open the sample video</a>.</video></div><figcaption>Saved analysis from an earlier project output. Play to load the video (about 85 MB). This illustrates the workflow; it does not establish reconstruction accuracy.</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section id="approach"><h2>Keep the evidence connected.</h2><ol class="case-process"><li><strong>Process locally.</strong><p>Detection, tracking, and calibration create observations from film. Resumable checkpoints make long processing runs recoverable.</p></li><li><strong>Review the uncertain parts.</strong><p>Source-clock alignment, court geometry, identity, and observation quality are checked before a sequence is approved.</p></li><li><strong>Publish a versioned view.</strong><p>The coaching interface connects film, spatial output, and annotations. Notes are scoped to workspace, session, event, and replay revision.</p></li></ol></section>
  <section id="evidence"><h2>From observations to space.</h2><p>Earlier saved outputs show player detections and team heatmaps. These are useful artifacts to inspect alongside the broader platform work.</p><div class="heatmap-viewer"><div class="heatmap-controls" role="group" aria-label="Select team heatmap"><button type="button" disabled data-team="0" aria-pressed="true">Team 0</button><button type="button" disabled data-team="1" aria-pressed="false">Team 1</button></div><figure data-heatmap="0"><img src={href('compvision/team_0_heatmap.png')} alt="Saved spatial heatmap for team 0 from an earlier CourtVision output" loading="lazy" width="1784" height="1031"/><figcaption>Team 0 · earlier saved output, not a current full-match reconstruction.</figcaption></figure><figure data-heatmap="1"><img src={href('compvision/team_1_heatmap.png')} alt="Saved spatial heatmap for team 1 from an earlier CourtVision output" loading="lazy" width="1784" height="1031"/><figcaption>Team 1 · earlier saved output, not a current full-match reconstruction.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="metric-grid"><div><strong>84</strong><span>Approved scoped replay windows</span></div><div><strong>358</strong><span>Field-goal records in the progress report</span></div><div><strong>274</strong><span>Records without approved replay</span></div></div><p class="resource-caption">Source: project progress report, September 11, 2026. These are coverage counts, not accuracy measurements.</p></section>
  <section id="limitations"><h2>Show what is ready.<br>Be clear about what is not.</h2><p>The approved windows remain partial reconstructions. Full-recording unattended reconstruction and an independent unseen-film trial remain unfinished. A rendered replay does not by itself validate a ball path, a named identity, or an articulated pose.</p><p>Current team films, private replay packages, labels, and player registries are not part of this public portfolio. The media here was already available in the earlier portfolio.</p></section>
  <section id="artifacts"><h2>Inspect a saved output.</h2><div class="resource-links"><a class="button button-dark" href={href('compvision/compvision-sample.mp4')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open annotated video ↗</a><a class="button" href={href('compvision/all_players.png')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open detection frame ↗</a></div></section>
</CaseLayout>
<script>
  const viewer = document.querySelector('.heatmap-viewer');
  if (viewer) {
    viewer.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-team]').forEach(button => button.disabled = false);
    viewer.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-heatmap="1"]')!.hidden = true;
    viewer.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-team]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      viewer.querySelectorAll('[data-team]').forEach(item => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)));
      viewer.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-heatmap]').forEach(figure => figure.hidden = figure.dataset.heatmap !== button.dataset.team);
    }));
  }
</script>
